# Custom applications

Generated standalone apps are the right default. Switch to authored `main.roc`
when you need custom routing, extra platform effects, or a shape the
generator does not cover. Reuse `.rocci` components either way.

Start with [Notes](/examples/notes/) for Roc-centered custom development
(`main.roc` plus Rocci templates). The [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/)
is the pattern gallery. [Snake](/examples/snake/) is the advanced
custom-runtime ceiling. [Rocci Blocks](/examples/blocks/) stays standalone;
it is not a `main.roc` app.

`rocci run examples/rocci/custom/notes --no-window` serves `/`.

## Directory apps

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/custom/notes --no-window
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/ | grep -E 'notes|Add'
```

`rocci run` on a directory compiles sibling `.rocci` modules and starts the
authored Roc program. `@get:view` / `@method:fragment` on those modules are
not the generated standalone dispatcher; `main.roc` owns HTTP.

Open [Notes](/examples/notes/) and use the sidebar source list.

The server still owns HTML. Datastar remains transport.

## Pattern gallery

The [Datastar gallery](/examples/datastar/) ports official Datastar
interaction patterns with authored `main.roc`:

| Route | What to notice |
| --- | --- |
| `/search` | `@let`, `@if`, `@for` |
| `/edit` | `@match` for editing |
| `/todos` | filters and lists |
| `/tabs` | lazy tabs |
| `/validate` | inline validation |

## Snake is the ceiling

[Snake](/examples/snake/) is an explicitly advanced **Datastar + Rocci
multiplayer stress demo**: a hand-written SSE unfold that morphs a full board
at ~8 Hz so you can watch live stream bandwidth. Do not copy that unfold into
ordinary apps; generated `@get:live` already emits the poll loop. Use Snake
when you need a custom ceiling the generator does not cover, or when you want
to measure morph cost. Do not treat [Rocci Blocks](/examples/blocks/) as a
custom-main example.

**Related:** [Applications](/docs/applications/),
[Package](/docs/applications/package/).
